		<name>Open Camera</name>
		<summary>Camera with multi-frame HDR, night mode, looks and manual controls</summary>
		<desc>Open Camera is a camera app built on CameraX and Camera2. Photos are processed on the device.

&lt;b&gt;Photo&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-frame HDR and Night: several frames are aligned and merged on the device&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Astro mode for long exposures on a tripod&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ultra HDR (JPEG_R) output on devices that support it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Looks, frames and a photo editor with object removal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pro mode with manual ISO, shutter, focus and white balance, and RAW (DNG) capture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;b&gt;Video and more&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Video modes, QR and barcode scanning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Device profiles that pick the right lenses on each phone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;b&gt;Privacy&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No network access by default. Optional models (for example object removal or denoise) are downloaded from the project's GitHub releases only after you confirm, and are checked against a SHA-256 hash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crash reports stay on the device unless you share them yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

RAW decoding for camera-maker files uses LibRaw (LGPL-2.1) as a separate shared library.
</desc>
